---
// Colophon (Build-Phase 6): how the site was built, what it uses, what it does
// not do. The license notices, the AI-art disclosure and the privacy line the
// Plan requires live here, in plain words. Indexable; linked from the footer.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RouteMark from '../components/RouteMark.astro';

const repo = 'https://github.com/RajatA98/RajatAroraPortfolio';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Colophon, Rajat Arora"
  description="How this site was built: Astro, one animated island, self-hosted type, no cookies, and the checks that run on every change."
>
  <article class="wrap colophon">
    <header class="intro">
      <RouteMark class="mark" />
      <h1>Colophon</h1>
      <p class="lede">How this site was built, what it uses, and what it does not do.</p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="built-title">
      <h2 id="built-title">Built as proof</h2>
      <p>
        The site is a static <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> build with strict TypeScript. One React island
        runs the animated voyage, and it loads <a href="https://gsap.com">GSAP</a> on demand, only on a wide screen with
        motion allowed. Phones and readers who prefer reduced motion get the same chapter as plain HTML and never
        download the animation code. Beyond that island, the only scripts are a small copy helper on the contact
        chapter and the performance beacon described below.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every change runs the same checks before it can ship: a type check, unit tests, a scan of the source and
        the build output for terms that must not appear, a JavaScript size budget, browser tests with keyboard,
        reduced-motion and accessibility checks, and Lighthouse budgets for bytes, layout shift and an accessibility
        score of 100. The thresholds are documented in the repository.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="type-title">
      <h2 id="type-title">Type</h2>
      <p>
        The typeface is Archivo by Omnibus-Type, used under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Two subsets are
        self-hosted here: an expanded 800 weight for display and a 400 to 500 range for text. No fonts are loaded
        from a third party.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="motion-title">
      <h2 id="motion-title">Motion</h2>
      <p>
        The voyage is animated with GSAP 3 and its ScrollTrigger plugin under the GSAP standard no-charge license.
        Everything else on the site only moves in answer to an action.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="art-title">
      <h2 id="art-title">Art</h2>
      <p>
        The route mark, the chart, the ports and the three ship drawings are original work made for this site. The
        portrait in the first chapter is a placeholder today. The planned portrait is an original character,
        AI-assisted and hand-finished. No franchise assets are used anywhere on the site, and a check for that runs
        on every build.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
      <h2 id="privacy-title">Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        No cookies, no trackers, no advertising. The only measurement is anonymous page-performance data collected
        by Vercel Speed Insights, which records how fast pages load and nothing about who you are. The contact
        details on the site are published on purpose, so that you can reach me.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="source-title">
      <h2 id="source-title">Source</h2>
      <p>
        The site is open source. The code, the tests and the checks are all in
        <a href={repo}>the repository on GitHub</a>, so the claims on this page can be read rather than taken on trust.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .colophon {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-6);
    padding-block: var(--s-8) 0;
    max-width: calc(var(--measure) + 2 * var(--gutter));
    margin-inline: 0;
  }

  .intro {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-4);
    justify-items: start;
  }

  .intro :global(.mark) {
    max-width: 10rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--t-4);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--t-2);
    margin-bottom: var(--s-3);
  }

  .lede,
  section p {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  section p + p {
    margin-top: var(--s-3);
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .colophon {
      margin-inline: auto;
    }
  }
</style>
